  "text": "Recipe: Chutney Sandwich with Lentil Wrap\nCreator: Kusum Dhairyawan\nCategory: Sandwich\nIngredients: cilantro, mint leaves, green chilli, curry leaves, lemon juice, ginger, garlic cloves, jeera, sesame seeds, kala namak, orange lentils, tomato, onion, cucumber, potatoes, beets, Chaat Masala\nCooking methods: no-cook, blend, saute, boil\nInstructions: (1) GREEN CHUTNEY Grind into fine consistency: cilantro, mint leaves, green chilli, curry leaves, lemon juice, a small piece of ginger, 2 garlic cloves, jeera, some sesame seeds & kala namak (optional). (2) LENTIL WRAPS Soak orange lentils for 4 hours, then grind into paste with some water. Let it ferment overnight. Next day, make a wrap on griddle just like we make dosa. (3) SANDWICH Spread GREEN CHUTNEY on wrap. Add thinly sliced vegetables like tomato, onion, cucumber, boiled potatoes & beets. Sprinkle some Chaat Masala. Cut in half.\nNotes: kala namak (optional)\nSub-recipes: Green Chutney, Lentil Wraps",
